<title>UK: KINGFISHER, DIXONS UP ON RETAIL SALES SURGE.</title>
<headline>KINGFISHER, DIXONS UP ON RETAIL SALES SURGE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in retailers Kingfisher and Dixons rose on Tuesday, benefiting from strong retail sales which showed the fastest growth in nine months.</p>
<p>Kingfisher rose 10-1/2p to 745p whilst Dixons gained 6-1/2p to 614-1/2p.</p>
<p>Earlier the British Retail Consortium said in its monthly survey that retail sales grew by 5.2 percent in the year to July.</p>
</text>
